# --- Du-Olhoff 2007 clean-room reproduction (development/reconstruction/Matlab/reproduction2007) ---
# The frozen baselines are the migration regression gate and the paper figures
# are inputs to the comparison plots, so they must be tracked despite the
# blanket *.mat / *.log / *.png / *.txt rules above.  Run-time output under
# its results/ directory stays ignored.
!development/reconstruction/Matlab/reproduction2007/baseline/*.mat
!development/reconstruction/Matlab/reproduction2007/baseline/*.log
!development/reconstruction/Matlab/reproduction2007/docs/figs/*.png
!development/reconstruction/Matlab/reproduction2007/SOURCE_SHA256.txt

# --- r3 Olhoff benchmark-path equivalence proofs (development/benchmark_history/examples_Performance/equivalence) ---
# These .mat records ARE the admission evidence for every Olhoff timing row:
# olhoff_equivalence_gate reads them to decide whether a mesh may enter a
# performance table.  Ignoring them under the blanket *.mat rule would leave the
# gate with nothing to read on a fresh clone.
!development/benchmark_history/examples_Performance/equivalence/*.mat
!development/benchmark_history/examples_Performance/equivalence/negative_controls/*.mat

# Phase 2I qualification evidence is an audit deliverable, not disposable run
# output.  Keep the CSV decision tables, checksum manifest, and the minimum raw
# records needed to reproduce the negative precision ruling on a fresh clone.
!development/experiments/iteration_efficiency/iteration_efficiency_phase2i_precision_qualification/*.csv
!development/experiments/iteration_efficiency/iteration_efficiency_phase2i_precision_qualification/SHA256SUMS.txt
!development/experiments/iteration_efficiency/iteration_efficiency_phase2i_precision_qualification/raw/*.csv
!development/experiments/iteration_efficiency/iteration_efficiency_phase2i_precision_qualification/raw/*.mat

# Archives.  Zip bundles are local backups of content that is either already
# tracked file-by-file or deliberately excluded; they are not evidence, and one
# of them (development/legacy_implementations/OlhoffArchive.zip, 552 MB) exceeds GitHub's 100 MB per-file
# hard limit and blocks the push outright.  Keep them on disk, out of git.
*.zip

# Paths above that point into development/ were re-pointed by the 2026-09-14
# repository cleanup (development/repository_cleanup/MIGRATION_MANIFEST.tsv).
